                <span class="pkg-chip">lang/id/</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="repo-footer">
            <a href="https://github.com/krewire/krewire.github.io/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="repo-action primary">Issues →</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/krewire/krewire.github.io/blob/main/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="repo-action secondary">Contributing ↗</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5-STEP CONTRIBUTOR GUIDE -->
  <section class="onboarding" id="guide">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-head w-full text-center flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
        <div class="sub-badge" data-i18n="guide.badge">Onboarding Fast-Track</div>
        <h2 data-i18n="guide.title">Start Contributing in 5 Steps</h2>
        <p data-i18n="guide.subtitle">From zero to your first merged pull request. Here is how to get your development environment running in minutes.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="quickstart-steps">
        <div class="qs-card">
          <div class="qs-num">1</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="guide.s1_title">1. Fork &amp; Clone Repositories</h3>
          <p data-i18n="guide.s1_desc">Fork any Krewire repository to your personal GitHub account, then clone it locally to begin:</p>
          <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/your-username/krewire
cd krewire</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="qs-card">
          <div class="qs-num">2</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="guide.s2_title">2. Initialize Workspace (go.work)</h3>
          <p data-i18n="guide.s2_desc">If working across multiple repos, synchronize your local Go workspace seamlessly with Go 1.27.1+:</p>
          <pre><code>go work init ./krewire ./krew ./cloud ./auth ./dash
go work sync</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="qs-card">
          <div class="qs-num">3</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="guide.s3_title">3. Pick an Open Issue</h3>
          <p data-i18n-html="guide.s3_desc_html">Browse our curated issues list tagged with <span class="tag-issue">good-first-issue</span> or <span class="tag-issue">help-wanted</span>. Comment to let maintainers know you are working on it.</p>
          <div class="mt-4">
            <a href="https://github.com/krewire/krewire/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+label%3Agood-first-issue" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" data-i18n="guide.s3_btn">View Good First Issues →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="qs-card">
          <div class="qs-num">4</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="guide.s4_title">4. Implement &amp; Verify Locally</h3>
          <p data-i18n="guide.s4_desc">Write clean, idiomatic Go code and tests. Verify that all 3 Quality Gates pass with zero failures:</p>
          <pre><code>gofmt -l .
go vet ./...
go test -race ./...</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="qs-card">
          <div class="qs-num">5</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="guide.s5_title">5. Submit PR with Conventional Commits</h3>
          <p data-i18n="guide.s5_desc">Open a PR following Conventional Commits (feat, fix, docs, refactor, test). Maintainers and AI Boost will review and guide you to merge.</p>
          <pre><code>git checkout -b feat/my-feature
git commit -m "feat(web): add handler (ref #123)"
git push origin feat/my-feature</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 AUTOMATED QUALITY GATES -->
  <section class="standards" id="standards">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-head w-full text-center flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
        <div class="sub-badge" data-i18n="standards.badge">Quality Assurance</div>
        <h2 data-i18n="standards.title">The Krewire Way: 3 Quality Gates</h2>
        <p data-i18n="standards.subtitle">To keep the codebase reliable, predictable, and production-ready, every pull request passes through three automated gates.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="gates-grid">
        <div class="gate-card">
          <div class="gate-icon">✓</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="standards.gate1_title">Gate 1: Format &amp; Lint</h3>
          <p data-i18n="standards.gate1_desc">Zero lint errors and idiomatic Go formatting. Code must adhere strictly to Go standard conventions.</p>
          <div class="gate-req" data-i18n="standards.gate1_req">Required: gofmt -l . (clean), go vet ./... (clean)</div>
        </div>

        <div class="gate-card">
          <div class="gate-icon">🛡️</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="standards.gate2_title">Gate 2: Race &amp; Tests</h3>
          <p data-i18n="standards.gate2_desc">Every commit is verified with race condition detection and comprehensive unit &amp; integration tests.</p>
          <div class="gate-req" data-i18n="standards.gate2_req">Required: 100% test pass, 0 data races</div>
        </div>

        <div class="gate-card">
          <div class="gate-icon">📝</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="standards.gate3_title">Gate 3: Spec &amp; Commits</h3>
          <p data-i18n="standards.gate3_desc">Changes must link to a valid Spec or Issue, following Conventional Commits format.</p>
          <div class="gate-req" data-i18n="standards.gate3_req">Required: Semantic commit format &amp; spec traceability</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PUBLIC GOVERNANCE & RFC FRAMEWORK (Issue #5) -->
  <section class="governance-section" id="governance">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-head w-full text-center flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
        <div class="sub-badge">Ecosystem Governance</div>
        <h2>Public RFC Workflow &amp; Architectural Decisions</h2>
        <p>Krewire operates under transparent open-source governance. All major architectural shifts follow the Request for Comments (RFC) process before becoming permanent Architectural Decision Records (ADRs).</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 4-PHASE RFC PROCESS -->
      <div class="rfc-steps-grid mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
        <div class="rfc-card p-5 border rounded-xl bg-surface">
          <div class="rfc-step-num text-xs font-bold text-primary mb-2">Phase 1</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-base mb-2">Proposal &amp; Problem</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted">Open a GitHub Discussion in <code>krewire/internal</code> outlining the motivation, trade-offs, and ecosystem impact.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rfc-card p-5 border rounded-xl bg-surface">
          <div class="rfc-step-num text-xs font-bold text-primary mb-2">Phase 2</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-base mb-2">Formal RFC Draft</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted">Submit an RFC PR using the standard template covering API design, failure modes, and migration plans.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rfc-card p-5 border rounded-xl bg-surface">
          <div class="rfc-step-num text-xs font-bold text-primary mb-2">Phase 3</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-base mb-2">14-Day Review</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted">Public comment period for Indonesian and global contributors to review, benchmark, and propose refinements.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rfc-card p-5 border rounded-xl bg-surface highlight-card">
          <div class="rfc-step-num text-xs font-bold text-primary mb-2">Phase 4</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-base mb-2">Consensus &amp; ADR</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted">Consensus among Maintainers promotes the RFC into an immutable ADR (e.g., ADR-6CAB8C) committed to <code>internal/</code>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- PUBLIC ADR DIGEST -->
      <div class="adr-digest-box mt-10">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-4">Canonical Architectural Decision Records (ADR Digest)</h3>
        <div class="adr-list flex flex-col gap-3">
          <div class="adr-item p-4 border rounded-lg bg-surface">
            <span class="adr-id font-bold text-primary">ADR-6CAB8C</span>: <strong>Ecosystem Architecture Baseline &amp; Strict Downward-Only Dependencies</strong>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-1">Defines strict unidirectional boundaries: <code>templates/boost → tools/kiw → pkg/* → pkg/model</code>. Zero upward edges allowed.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="adr-item p-4 border rounded-lg bg-surface">
            <span class="adr-id font-bold text-primary">ADR-C9L2P</span>: <strong>Multi-Workload Single Binary Dispatch</strong>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-1">Standardizes 8 workload kinds behind <code>krewire.yaml</code> and unified CLI <code>kiw</code> with zero framework lock-in.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="adr-item p-4 border rounded-lg bg-surface">
            <span class="adr-id font-bold text-primary">ADR-D1F3N</span>: <strong>Zero-Trust Defense-in-Depth Edge Security</strong>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-1">Requires CSRF token verification, ACME automated TLS, token bucket rate limiting, and secure HTTP response headers across all daemons.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- CODE OF CONDUCT & SECURITY REPORTING -->
      <div class="coc-security-grid mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="p-6 border rounded-xl bg-surface">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-base mb-2">📜 Contributor Covenant Code of Conduct (v2.1)</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted mb-3">We pledge to make participation in Krewire a harassment-free experience for everyone, regardless of age, body size, visible or invisible disability, ethnicity, sex characteristics, gender identity, or experience level.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/krewire/.github/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-sm text-primary font-bold">Read Full Code of Conduct (EN/ID) →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 border rounded-xl bg-surface">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-base mb-2">🔒 Security Vulnerability Reporting</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted mb-3">Never open a public issue for suspected security vulnerabilities. Please report any potential vulnerability responsibly via our encrypted reporting channel.</p>
          <p class="text-sm font-mono text-primary">security@krewire.com (PGP key in internal/docs/security/)</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

